  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_011 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) at 0.530 acc, and the multimodal multiprofile config_019 (same but +resnet50, weighted fusion) only reaches 0.525, suggesting the image adds little with avgpool aggregation. The dominant design question now is whether a more expressive aggregation (transformer vs. avgpool) can improve the multiprofile representation that drives most of the performance gain. Question: config_032 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, transformer) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_011, isolating the aggregation strategy. Why this is best: If transformer aggregation helps, it identifies a concrete lever to push past 0.530 and informs whether to pair it with multimodal fusion in later experiments. If it does not, we can rule out that direction and focus budget on image encoder quality or fusion strategy. Either outcome reduces uncertainty about an important design axis with one experiment, making it the highest-information next step under the limited budget."
